                                                                            1/7
Code 5 -- Slurs, brackets, 1st ending, etc. --

                           ษอออออออออออหอออออออออออป
  parameter structure:     บ     p1    บ     p2    บ
                           บ code num. บ staff num.บ
                           ศอออออออออออสอออออออออออผ
            ฺฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฟ
            ณ                 ฺฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฤฟ               ณ
 ษออออออออออฯอออออออออหอออออออฯอออออออออออหออออออออฯออออออออหออออออฯออออออออป
 บ         p3         บ       p4          บ        p5       บ      p6       บ
 บleft horizontal pos.บ left vertical pos.บ right vert. pos.บ rt. horz. pos.บ
 ศออออออออออออออออออออสอออออออออออออออออออสอออออออออออออออออสอออออออออออออออผ

 ษอออออออออออหออออออออหออออออออออออหออออออออออออออหออออออออออหออออออออออออออป
 บ    p7     บ   p8   บ     p9     บ     p10      บ   p11    บ     p12      บ
 บ curvature บ offset บ flattening บ curve center บ dash/dot บ change direc.บ
 ศอออออออออออสออ(num)อสอออ(num)ออออสออออออออออออออสออออออออออสออออออออออออออผ

 ษอออออออออออหอออออออหออออออหออออออออหอออออออออออออหออออออออออออออหอออออออออป
 บ    p13    บ  p14  บ  p15 บ  p16   บ    p17      บ    p18       บ   p19   บ
 บ thickness บ start บ stop บ number บ num. lft-rt บ num. up-down บfine tuneบ
 ศอออออออออออสอออออออสออออออสออออออออสอออออออออออออสออออออออออออออสอออออออออผ

*
                                                                            2/7
  P7 = amount of curvature (in scale steps).  A positive number makes the
       slur curve upwards, a negative number makes the slur curve downwards
       (i.e. the center of the slur will be lower than the ends).

  P8 = horizontal offset.

     P8 =  0 or 10 = slur will begin exactly at P3 position and end at
                     P6 position (i.e. at the left edge of notes).
        = -1 or 11 = slur ends are centered over notes at positions of
                     P3 and P6.
        = -2 or 12 = slur falls between notes at pos. P3 and P6. (tied notes)
        = -3 or 13 = same as -2, but extra space for 1st note being dotted.
        = -4 or 14 = center slur ends on right edge of note.
        = -5 or 15 = middle of 1st to end of last note.
        = -6 or 16 = end of 1st note to middle of last note.
        = -7 or 17 = middle of 1st note to start of last note.
        = -8 or 18 = start of 1st note to middle of last note.
        = -9 or 19 = start of 1st note to end of last note.
        = .02 to .99 = places the left end of the slur a percentage of the
                    distance from the front of the 1st note to 2 note widths
                    to the right.  The right end of the slur is placed in the
                    converse position in regard to the last note.

*
                                                                            3/7

     P8 = 1 = 1st ending, P8 = 2 = 2nd ending.
                 P7 sets height of bracket -- should usually = c.5 or 6.
          
          If P9 is positive, then P9 sets the ending number.
                  For 1st ending with open bracket to right: P8=2, P9=1.
          
          P8=1, P9 = -1 = no number, bracket open to the left        
                   = -2 = no number, complete bracket     
          P8=2, P9 = -1 = no number, bracket open to the right       

          The 'CN n' command (center) will move the ends of 1st and 2nd
          endings to positions of nearest bar lines.  If the bar line
          starts from a staff below, the staff number (n) must be given.

             

             * For PAGE program --with 1st-2nd ending:

                 P5 = 100 =put ending in ALL parts, = 200 =in NO parts.



*
                                                                            4/7
     
     P8 = 3 = broken bracket with the number 3 in center. (P11=0)
           P9  = set the number (if number other than 3 is needed.)
           P10 = move the number to the left or right of center.
             P10 =  0 = default (.5) = number is centered.
                 = .3 = number is 30% distance from left to right.
                 = .8 =   "    "  80%    "      "    "   "    "
              P11 = 1 = continuous bracket with number inside.
                  = 2 =      "        "     "     "    outside.
                  = 3 = bracket with NO number. (P8 must = 3 for all these.) 
              P17 and P18 can move the number left-right, up-down.

      
      P9 = slur flattening factor.  Longer slurs often should be flattened
               in the middle.  By setting P9 to a positive value, a larger
               portion of the slur will be flat.  Negative values will
               decrease the flat area.

      P9 with brackets and endings:
          P8 = 1 and P9 = -1 = continuation of 1st ending.
          P8 = 3 and P9 <= -2 = open space in bracket (for |--- 3:5 ---| etc.)


*      
                                                                            5/7
      P10 = set center of curvature.  When P10 is left at zero the default
              value of .5 is in effect.  If P10 is less than .5 the center
              of curvature shifts to the left.  Values greater than .5 shift
              the center to the right.  P10 also moves number in bracket.

      P11 = 1 = slur is made up of dashes. (P8=0)
              If P11 is greater than 1, then P11 = number of dashes in slur.

      P11 =-1 = slur is made up of dots.
              If P11 is less than -4, then P11 = number of dots in slur.
                          (Even numbers only.)


      P12 = half or reversed slurs.
              P12 = 1 = the slur shape will be as if only the left half
                      were being drawn.
              P12 = 2 = only the right half shape appears.
              P12 = -1 causes the slur to reverse direction at its midpoint
                      (see P10).  If P7 is positive, the 1st part of the
                      curve will be up.  If P7 is negative the 1st part of
                      the curve will be down.  (The slur length must be
                      visually adjusted when P12 = -1.)

*
                                                                            6/7
      P13 = thickness control.  Zero = normal thickness (100%).
              P13 = .6 = 60% of normal.  P13 = 1.3 = 130% of normal, etc.

      P14 & P15 are used to break up slurs to avoid crossing over other items.
              The slur first should be set up with its normal parameter values
              in P3, P4, P5, and P6.  Then P14 can set where the visible
              portion of the slur STARTS and P15 can set where the visible
              portion ENDS.  P14 = .3 = visible part starts 30% of the way
              through.  P15 = .65 = visible part ends 65% of the way through,
              etc.  P14 and P15 can be used separately or together.

      P16 = a number to be put in the middle of a broken slur.  (For triplets,
              etc.) If the number is NEGATIVE, it will appear (positive) just
              below an unbroken slur whose curve is up, or just above a slur
              whose curve is down.

      P17 = can move the number given in P16 left or right.
      P18 = can move the number given in P16 up or down.
              (These parameters must be used if the slur is quite steep.)
  **************************************
  Offsets:  P16=1, P17=absolute left offset, P18=absolute right offset.
       P8 will be ignored - also then other uses of p16,17,18 are not valid.

*
                                                                            7/7

      P19 = fine tune slur thickening. P19 may control the position through
            the drawing of the first half of the slur where it reaches its
            maximum thickness. The default is P19 = 0 = .85 = 85%. This
            might be used (in conjunction with P13) for very short ties or
            nearly vertical slurs. (Use the SHOW feature while editing.)


ออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออออ


Guitar tremolo bar slides: P9 = 99
       
       All the parameters here work just like those for slurs except that 
       only the upper 2 vectors of a triangle will appear instead of the 
       curve of a slur.

       If P7 = 0, only a straight line will appear.

       For thicker lines, set P13 = 1, 2, or 3.


